# Testing (Pest)

- Feature tests cover happy path + primary failure/auth cases for changed behavior
- Use factories (`Model::factory()`), not manual `Model::create([...])` attribute dumps
- Use `RefreshDatabase` (or equivalent isolation) when touching the DB
- HTTP tests assert status, JSON/structure, and authorization outcomes
- Queue/job tests use `Queue::fake()` / `Bus::fake()` when relevant
- Prefer asserting behavior (status, DB, events) over framework internals
- Descriptions: `it('guest cannot view draft post')` — plain English
- Mirror structure: `tests/Feature/...` for HTTP/Livewire; `tests/Unit/...` for Actions/Services/Repos

```php
it('stores a blog post', function () {
    $user = User::factory()->create();

    $this->actingAs($user)
        ->post(route('blog_posts.store'), [...])
        ->assertRedirect();

    $this->assertDatabaseHas('blog_posts', [...]);
});
```
